{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792338757,"nonce":"7YlQKfkDr+olDx8WKujzY2jNNNs=","title":"Python: an isinstance branch does not narrow a dynamic name, and an uncalled function's parameter widens what it writes","message":"decimal.py made every Decimal field and the module's _context dynamic. In Decimal.__init__, self.coefficient = value.coefficient under isinstance(value, Decimal) read value dynamically, since value joins an int and a Decimal. setcontext(context), never called, had its parameter settled to Object, and the pass that re-reads global writes with settled signatures joined that into _context, so _context.prec and every exponent computed from it were dynamic. telco spent about a third of its samples in dynamic integer arithmetic. Fix: the sugar pass gives an isinstance(x, C) branch, C a class of the module, x = x and its assert, which the typer reads as an instance; a closed module function no call reaches is left out of the global-writes pass. NUC, 4 pinned cores, CI's figure, 9 reps: telco 0.466, spectral-norm 0.893, json 0.952, the rest within noise (raytrace, fft, LU and hexiom2 re-run at 15 reps: 0.98 to 1.01). Mac: telco 12.9 to 4.6 ms an iteration.","files":null}]}